First-pass horizontal overlay UX update

- Horizontal overlays now show tabs for the current browser window only; a window-switcher icon appears only when other windows exist and opens a picker to switch to them.
- In the compact horizontal strip, tabs flex between a readable minimum of 112px and a maximum of 220px, then scroll if more tabs cannot fit.
- When the horizontal bar is expanded to 72px or taller, tabs use a scrollable multirow grid instead of stretching across a single row.
- Tab visuals are inset on a non-interactive surface while the tab wrapper remains the full click/drag target, preserving clicks near the screen edge.
- Kept toolbar orientation tied to the overlay edge and left vertical/windowed layouts unchanged.

Validation: content.js passes JavaScript syntax parsing; CSS braces are balanced; manifest and script references remain unchanged. No live browser UI test was run.
